{"id":"u-4c570a15-d5e8-4cb0-ba89-43930599dcda","src":"community","title":"12-Week Hybrid Athlete: Strength & Conditioning","author":"Gunnu","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/KVv8Mr-12-week-hybrid-athlete-program","desc":"The 12-Week Hybrid Athlete program is designed to develop strength, muscle mass, conditioning, and overall athletic performance through a structured, progressive training plan.\n\nCombining compound strength movements, hypertrophy-focused accessory work, conditioning intervals, and core training, this program targets a balanced physique while building a stronger and more capable athlete.\n\nTRAINING SPLIT\n• Monday — Lower Body A: Squat Strength & Leg Development\n• Tuesday — Upper Body A: Strength\n• Wednesday — Conditioning & Core\n• Thursday — Lower Body B: Posterior Chain & Leg Hypertrophy\n• Friday — Upper Body B: Hypertrophy & Arms\n• Saturday — Optional Recovery & Mobility\n• Sunday — Rest\n\n12-WEEK PROGRESSION\nThe program begins with a foundation phase to establish technique and consistency, progresses through structured strength and hypertrophy training, and incorporates a deload week to manage fatigue. The later phases focus on progressive overload, improved work capacity, and consolidated performance.\n\nHOW TO PROGRESS\nTrack every working set in Boostcamp. Progress by increasing repetitions or load when you can complete all prescribed sets with sound technique and the target effort. Not every week requires heavier weights; recovery and performance determine when to progress.\n\nWHO IS IT FOR?\nDesigned for trainees with gym experience who want to develop a stronger, more muscular, and better-conditioned physique through consistent training.\n\nIMPORTANT\nChoose loads and exercise variations appropriate to your ability. Adapt training for individual limitations, and seek qualified medical or rehabilitation guidance when needed. Athletic activities such as sprinting and jumping should be introduced only when appropriately prepared 